# Level 21 by password VXBB -- variant 1, which is one neighbour rather than ten
# -- rescued, walked out through the exit door, and into level 22.
#
# The first movie in the corpus that finishes a level and crosses into the next,
# and it exists to measure one word. `$80:866F` seeds the next level's victim
# gate from the rescue counts (`LDA $1F9C : SED : ADC $1F9E : STA $1D50 : STA
# $1D52`), and `$80:8947` clears those counts one call before each load, so the
# gate should carry the score of the level just played and nothing else.
#
# It does. `$1E7C` steps 21 -> 22 at frame 4950, `$1F9C` is cleared at 5450, and
# level 22 loads with `$1D50 = $0001` and `$7E:6E30 = 1`: one victim placed out
# of the ten its record holds.
#
# Two things cost an attempt each and are worth knowing before editing this.
# Tile (51,148) is water -- row y=1190 is wet from x=414 to x=432 and row y=1180
# is dry across -- so the staircase out of (504,1196) has to be crossed a row
# high, in hops short enough that the fitter cannot drift into it. And the level
# does not end when the counter reaches zero: an exit door (id `$37`, handler
# `$82:F958`) spawns, here at (374,780), and the player has to walk onto it.
#
# The four events that do that -- Down at 4464, Left at 4480 -- are hand-written.
# `fit_route.py` will not land on the door: aimed at it, it spent 51 legs and
# gave up at (366,782), through the right column and two pixels off the row.
